      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Luigi.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. XP ledger: level 5, power rating 13 → a level 5 Ranger player-character sheet (a player may take this seat; the authored CR 4 stands in where the ledger is silent). Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Reluctant Ghostbuster</strong> — Mushroom Kingdom / Mages' Guild (Contractor)</p><p>Status: Active — recovered alive from Bowser's lava-moat tunnels, treated at Dr. Toad's Star Hill Clinic, and under a two-week rest order; Mario remains absent.; as of 2 Aethel, 1035 BF reported — unverified — to be in the clinic's 'private wing, high security, consciousness fluxing', while something wearing his clothes stood outside in three copies</p><p>Luigi is the reluctant ghostbuster, the brother left behind by every heroic story that needed Mario in front, and the man whose history now carries the unresolved shadow of Mr. L, Guild contracts, haunted technology, medical testimony, and a disappearance mystery too large to fit inside the word sidekick. Waluigi finds Luigi infuriating, sympathetic, suspicious, brave, evasive, and extremely bad at choosing restful employment. The Poltergust is not just a vacuum; it is Luigi's proof that fear can be weaponized into duty. The Garden Above the Fire confirms that Luigi survived the lava-falls aftermath, recalled the line 'The star is not lost. Find the garden above the fire,' and reached Dr. Toad's clinic alive — still wounded, still asking for Mario, but no longer missing in the compound tunnels.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Poltergust Strobe &amp; Suction</strong> — “Professor E. Gadd's paratechnology turns Luigi's terror into steps: strobe, suction, containment, breathe, scream, continue.”</li><li><strong>Flashlight Strobe</strong> — “Luigi performed useful work: stunning ghosts, vacuuming threats, opening doors, and containing things he refused to discuss later.”</li><li><strong>Fear as Method</strong> — “Luigi relies on fear processed into procedure.”</li><li><strong>Containment Procedure</strong> — “Luigi performed useful work: stunning ghosts, vacuuming threats, opening doors, and containing things he refused to discuss later.”</li><li><strong>Guild Contractor</strong> — “Luigi arrived at the Ruined Manor under Guild contract.”</li><li><strong>The Shadow Called L</strong> — “Luigi is the reluctant ghostbuster, the brother left behind by every heroic story that needed Mario in front, and the man whose history now carries the unresolved shadow of Mr. L, Guild contracts, haunted technology”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/luigi</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/luigi</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
